 "applies_to": "Vertiv Liebert GXE3 UPS systems.",
 "summary": "The Liebert GXE3 UPS reports to a BMS through a Liebert IntelliSlot card (BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP). Analog Values carry input, bypass, output and battery measurements, Binary Values carry UPS events, and Multi-state Values carry system status, output source and settings. Objects are created when the card discovers the UPS.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP",
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "Tables 5.162, 5.163, 5.164, pdf pages 2159-2166 of the 2024 guide (printed page numbers are 4 lower).",
  "Object names are Vertiv data IDs (e.g. 5331_1); the description holds the guide's data label. Labels repeated for different sensors or circuits get the group name in brackets.",
  "Most temperature objects come in pairs: a °C object and a °F object (name ending _deg_F), usually at instance + 10000."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "Liebert IntelliSlot Modbus/BACnet Reference Guide (Modbus RTU and TCP, BACnet MSTP and IP)",
